==English==
{{wp}}

===Etymology===
{{ety|en|:inh|enm:streke<ety:inh<ang:strica<ety:inh<gmw-pro:*striki>>>>|tree=1}}
From {{inh|en|enm|streke}}, from {{inh|en|ang|strica}}, from {{inh|en|gem-pro|*strikiz}}, from {{der|en|ine-pro|*streyg-||line}}. Related to {{cog|frr|strijck}}, {{cog|osx|striki}}, {{cog|gml|streke}}, {{cog|nds|streek}}, {{cog|da|streg}}, {{cog|sv|streck}}, {{cog|nb,nn|strek}}, {{cog|is|stryk}}, {{m|is|strykr}}, {{cog|nl|streek}}, {{cog|af|streek}}, {{cog|goh|strih}}, {{cog|de|Strich}}, {{cog|got|𐍃𐍄𐍂𐌹𐌺𐍃}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/stɹiːk/}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-streak.ogg|a=US}}
* {{rhymes|en|iːk|s=1}}

===Noun===
{{wikidata lexeme|L221432}}
{{en-noun}}

# An irregular line, as is left from [[smear]]ing or [[motion]].
#* {{RQ:Lincoln Pratt's Patients|chapter=1|passage='Twas early June, the new grass was flourishing everywheres, the posies in the yard—peonies and such—in full bloom, the sun was shining, and the water of the bay was blue, with light green '''streaks''' where the shoal showed.}}
#: {{ux|en|The picture I took out the car window had '''streaks'''.}}
## A band, line or stripe.
##: {{ux|en|A '''streak''' of light on the horizon.}}
# A continuous [[series]] of like events.
#: {{near-syn|en|chain (''A [[series]] of interconnected things.'')|string (''A series of [[item]]s or [[event]]s; items arranged in a line; a trend; a sequence of words, letters, sounds, etc.'')}}
#: {{ux|en|I hope I can keep up this '''streak''' of accomplishments.}}
#: {{ux|en|I was on a winning '''streak''' until the fourth game, when I was dealt terrible cards.}}
## {{lb|en|social media|Internet}} A measure of activity that tracks how many consecutive days a certain interaction with another user or a service has taken place, a form of [[gamification]] to drive user engagement.
##* {{RQ:FT|edition=weekend|author=Jo Ellison|date=2025-05-31|title=The beguiling charm of a bedtime phone call|section=Life & Arts|page=20|passage=Out went conversation in favour of fast and more immediate pleasures. We migrated on to texts, voice notes, emojis and the Snapchat “'''streak'''”.}}
## {{lb|en|figurative}} A [[consistent]] [[facet]] of somebody's [[personality]].
##: {{ux|en|a mean '''streak'''}}
##: {{ux|en|a stubborn '''streak'''}}
##* {{RQ:Bramah Bravo of London|passage=But speaking of cats, there's a good deal to be learned about women from them, 'Orace. {{...}} I've known very few who wouldn't admit, between ourselves, that most others had a fair '''streak''' of the feline.}}
## A [[tendency]] or [[characteristic]], but not a [[dominant]] or [[pervasive]] one.
##: {{ux|en|She's a quiet, bookish person, but she has a rebellious '''streak'''.}}
# {{lb|en|geology}} The color of the [[powder]] of a [[mineral]], so called, because a simple field test for a mineral is to streak it against unglazed white porcelain.
# {{lb|en|biology}} A [[moth]] of the family {{taxfmt|Geometridae|family}}, {{taxlink|Chesias legatella|species}}.
#* {{pedia|Streak (moth)}}
# {{lb|en|shipbuilding}} A [[strake]].
# A [[rung]] or [[round]] of a [[ladder]].
# The act of streaking, or running naked through a public area.
# {{lb|en|collective}} A group of [[tiger]]s.
#: {{syn|en|ambush}}

