===Verb===
{{wikidata lexeme|L333157}}
{{en-verb}}

# {{lb|en|intransitive}} To have or obtain streaks.
#: {{ux|en|If you clean a window in direct sunlight, it will streak.}}
# {{lb|en|intransitive}} To run quickly.
#* {{RQ:Lindsay Age of Consent|year=1962|page=82|passage="As it was I came a hell of a crack against a Dam' rustic arbour in the garden. Dam' near stunned me. But I never stopped a second. Up and over the back fence and '''streaked''' for the common."}}
# {{lb|en|intransitive}} To run [[naked]] in public.
#: {{cot|en|flash}}
#: {{ux|en|It was a pleasant game until some guy went '''streaking''' across the field.}}
# {{lb|en|intransitive}} To move [[very]] [[swiftly]].
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To create streaks upon.
#: {{syn|en|vein}}
#: {{ux|en|You will '''streak''' a window by cleaning it in direct sunlight.}}
#* {{RQ:Melville Moby-Dick|chapter=32|page=157|passage=Though his entire back down to his side fins is of a deep sable, yet a boundary line, distinct as the mark in a ship’s hull, called the “bright waist,” that line '''streaks''' him from stem to stern, with two separate colours, black above and white below.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|journal=w:National Geographic|year=1990|month=August|volume=178|number=2|title=Neptune: Voyager's Last Picture Show|author=Rick Gore|page=35
|text=Wispy high clouds also '''streak''' Neptune's upper atmosphere.}}
# {{lb|en|obsolete|UK|Scotland}} To stretch; to extend; hence, to lay out, as a dead body. <!--related to "stretch"-->

